      "id": 40,
      "relativePath": "discordbot.bat",
      "description": "Launcher script for the Discord bot. Edit this if you need a specific Python path or want to run NodeJS instead.",
      "template": "@echo off\ntitle TCAdmin v3 Discord Bot Runner\ncls\n\necho ===================================================\necho TCAdmin v3 Discord Bot Launcher\necho ===================================================\necho.\n\n:: Ensure we are operating in the script\u0027s actual directory\ncd /d \u0022%~dp0\u0022\n\n:: Step 1: Check if Node.js is installed\nwhere node \u003Enul 2\u003Enul\nif %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n    echo [ERROR] Node.js is not installed or not in your system PATH!\n    echo Please install Node.js from https://nodejs.org before running.\n    echo.\n    exit /b 1\n)\n\n:: Step 2: Check if node_modules exists, install if missing\nif not exist \u0022node_modules\\\u0022 (\n    echo [INFO] node_modules folder missing. Installing dependencies...\n    call npm install --no-audit --no-fund\n    if %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n        echo [ERROR] Failed to install dependencies via npm.\n        exit /b 1\n    )\n    echo [SUCCESS] Dependencies installed successfully.\n    echo.\n)\n\n:: Step 3: Run the JavaScript Bot Script\necho [STARTING] Launching bot.js...\necho.\nnode bot.js\n\n:: If the bot crashes, exit with an error code so TCAdmin logs the failure\nif %errorlevel% neq 0 (\n    echo.\n    echo [CRASH] The bot has stopped executing with error code %errorlevel%.\n    echo.\n    exit /b %errorlevel%\n)\n\nexit /b 0",
      "order": 0,
      "enableEditor": false,
      "editor": []
    }
